SM(453,{"n":"Acts 5","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Acts 5.mp3","d":2822.3,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.2,"In just a minute, we'll be uh picking up in Acts of the Apostles chapter 5, verse 12."],[28.08,"And I'll say my usual that by the time people are hearing this on the internet, uh, the first Bible study on the book of Acts will be also available there."],[37.6,"And so you'll be able to go back and listen to that if you want to hear my introduction to the whole book."],[42.32,"Uh, to get us caught up sort of to where we are now."],[46.4,"We're still in the very early chapters of the Acts of the Apostles."],[50.64,"Uh, what we've been reading about most recently has been sort of the way of life of the early Christian community."],[56.4,"Uh, we've seen that uh the life of the early Christian. community in Jerusalem is a continuation of the life of Christ, the way that St"],[67.48,"Luke is presenting it."],[68.6,"Remember at the very beginning of Acts 1, he said that in the previous book he had talked about all that Jesus had begun to do and teach, and so now the apostles and the early Christian community are sort of continuing."],[82.92,"And that's been in both good and bad ways."],[85.56,"So we've seen since the coming of the Holy Spirit, we've seen the Apostles doing miracles like the miracles that Jesus did."],[92.04,"We've seen them teaching even in the temple, the way Jesus taught."],[97.08,"And we've also seen the Jewish authorities who had previously put Jesus to death also beginning to come after the apostles as they were hauled before the Sanhedrin."],[104.84,"And so it's a continuation in both both of those ways"],[112.32,"And this is what Jesus promised would happen, remember."],[115.84,"Most recently when we were going through the Gospel of John, remember Jesus said to his disciples, you know, if the world hated me, it will hate you."],[124.16,"You know, if they persecuted me, they will persecute you."],[126.88,"If they heard me and listened to me, they'll listen to you."],[129.6,"You know, and so this is exactly sort of what he was preparing them for."],[134.8,"Now we also saw telegraphed in the story of the ascension, as Saint Luke retold it at the beginning of Acts, that there's sort of this mission plan that they're gonna take the gospel of Christ and proclaim it in Jerusalem and then Judea and then Samaria and then out to the to the edge of the earth."],[149.76,"We're still in Jerusalem right now"],[156.28,"So we're still in the first sort of stage of that plan."],[160.52,"And immediately before we left off last time, we saw, and we talked about how this was sort of parallel to what happened in Leviticus."],[167.32,"Then in Leviticus, uh after God's presence came into the tabernacle, uh uh Aaron's two sons, Nadab and Abahu, uh, decided to sort of take this whole situation lightly and ended up being struck dead, um, to sort of show the community that this was now a serious thing, that God was living in their midst."],[187.56,"And in the same sort of way we saw last time that after the Holy Spirit comes to indwell the apostles and the members of the early Christian community, we saw Ananias and Sapphira who took that sort of lightly and thought they could lie to the community and try to present themselves as something other than what they were."],[206.48,"And St. Peter pointed out to them that they hadn't just lied to human beings, but they had lied to the Holy Spirit, who was now indwelling the community, and so because of that they dropped dead and were carried out."],[221.2,"And so we left off on that sort of happy note last time."],[227.2,"And now as we pick up again, we're gonna again be talking about and looking at sort of the life of this early community in Jerusalem where it is still together."],[238.72,"We've seen it grow from about 120 people to what were we at?"],[244.28,"We were at about 8,000."],[247.72,"So it's gotten much bigger, this community, but we're still talking about a community within Jerusalem at this time."],[256.84,"So unless we have any comments or questions or anything else, we'll go ahead and get started in Acts 5, verse 12."],[265.16,"And through the hands of the apostles, many signs and wonders were done among the people."],[269.32,"And they were all with one accord in Solomon's porch."],[272.76,"Yet none of the rest dared join them, but the people esteemed them highly."],[279.52,"So the miracle, remember that Saints Peter and John, when they were on the way into the temple to pray, they saw the paralyzed man begging and they healed him."],[291.36,"That wasn't sort of a one off."],[293.9,"So the way that we we read in the Gospels that Jesus, you know, we read about particular healings where he heals particular peoples, but that also just a lot of times in the Gospels it says, and Jesus went and healed the sick and drove out demons."],[309.96,"This was a regular thing."],[311.73,"As he traveled and ministered."],[314.21,"The same thing is happening on with happening now with the apostles."],[318.17,"This wasn't just one isolated incident, but this is a regular thing that people are being healed, these things are happening in the community, and there are signs and wonders."],[328.21,"We talked in John about the word sign in particular, that these miracles weren't just sort of a neat thing, like wow, you know, to draw attention, but that they were signs, the way a sign indicates something."],[343.23,"We talked about how the signs Jesus worked indicated that he was the Messiah and that the Messianic Age was sort of beginning."],[349.95,"Now this is the same kind of thing."],[351.87,"The fact that these things are happening, people are being healed, these things are happening, is a sign to the people around that within this community, within this uh gathering in uh Jerusalem, this age, you know, is is beginning to take shape, that the kingdom of God is sort of coming into the world beginning here."],[373.23,"I'm I'm puzzled by something I'm sure you can get to here"],[379.91,"It says, yet none of the rest dared join them, but the people esteemed them highly."],[385.43,"And then it says, and believers were increasingly added."],[388.63,"So who are the people who don't dare join them?"],[391.21,"Well, this is um Remember, notes it says through the hands of the apostles, many signs and wonders were done among the people, and they were all with one accord in Solomon's porch."],[404.67,"So Solomon's porch is a portion of the temple, as we were mentioning earlier."],[408.83,"Meaning they're not doing this."],[410.83,"Remember, they were hiding in a room."],[413.23,"They're not hiding in a room anymore."],[415.47,"Christian community isn't off somewhere hiding, and you know."],[418.95,"It's a big room if there are 8,000."],[420.69,"And people sort of people sort of come."],[422.77,"Is this the secret meeting?"],[424.05,"You know. I've I've got you know leprosy."],[427.33,"Can I get healed."],[428.3,"You know, or something off somewhere."],[430.38,"But this is being done publicly in full view."],[433.52,"Which it also makes sense if these are supposed to be signs."],[436.78,"So these are supposed to be things that the people of the city of Jerusalem are supposed to see."],[441.84,"And be drawn to it."],[442.64,"And there's sort of evidence that as these people are preaching that Jesus is the Messiah, because look, all these things that were supposed to happen when the Messiah comes are happening."],[453.32,"You know, so when they say Jesus is the Messiah, they must be telling the truth, is the idea."],[457.92,"So the others would be other members of the Christian community."],[460.24,"of So the apostles are all out there in force, sort the leadership doing these things."],[467.88,"But there are a lot of members of the Christian community who, because of the resistance that has already happened."],[474.86,"There aren't 8,000 people in Solomon's porch all doing these things."],[480.79,"But but there's so there's there's uh that's sort of telegraphing something that's coming up very soon in. Jerusalem, like an estimate number, how many people were in Jerusalem around that time"],[496.07,"Since 8,000, that's a big number already for Jerusalem."],[498.95,"Yeah, it well, it varies a lot depending on what time of year it is."],[504.59,"Because Jerusalem at this point, you know, was different than Jerusalem now, because of course at that point the temple was there."],[512.67,"And so at that point, when you had Passover, when you had Pentecost, especially Passover, but other feasts too, Pentecost, Feast of Tabernacle, all these other feasts, Jews would come from all over the world."],[525.47,"And so it's estimated, and a lot of these things are rough and we can't prove it, you know."],[530.91,"But it's it's estimated, and and and we're not just talking about Jerusalem proper, the city, but there are all these like Bethany and all these other villages that we've seen talked about all around it, you know."],[542.11,"Uh it's estimated that some of these years at Posca, at Passover, uh, there could be a million people in the area around."],[549.47,"A lot of them would have been camping essentially"],[552.15,"Million? You know, that's who would sort of flood and get packed into the city."],[559.91,"That's why when when that's why everyone was so worried when Jesus came there at Passover."],[566.07,"Because there's all these people packed into the city."],[568.79,"And you've got that many people packed into an area."],[572.31,"It's real easy for things like riots and you know, and things to get started."],[577.51,"You know, if you've got somebody going there preaching something, you know, that the kingdom of God is coming, you know, they might cause trouble with the Roman, you know."],[586.31,"You don't want a riot to break out."],[587.83,"And that's also why, as we saw, uh Pilate was so quick to go ahead and even though he didn't think Jesus was guilty of anything, to just execute him."],[594.63,"Because he was worried that a riot was beginning"],[596.27,"Yeah. That a riot could break out if he didn't sort of do what they wanted him to do."],[604.11,"And so he went ahead and did it."],[606.51,"Because things could very quickly get out of hand with that many people."],[610.99,"So at a normal time, I mean at Pentecost, again, we read that there was this huge crowd there of Jews from all over the world."],[619.07,"Not that many."],[621.61,"And we're now after that."],[623.61,"So we're probably talking about in terms of actual residents, there were probably maybe a hundred and fifty thousand actually in Jerusalem."],[634.77,"At this time."],[635.69,"That would make it a very big scene."],[637.21,"It was very big."],[638.09,"It was very big."],[638.81,"It makes sense"],[639.81,"Um that's including people who lived outside of the city."],[642.46,"In the villages and all that."],[643.66,"Yeah, yeah. The villages and all that."],[646.06,"It was it was very it was very big at the time because it was this hub."],[651.02,"And uh it gets, you know, sort of squashed by the Romans."],[658.06,"Um but yeah, it was it was very big."],[660.86,"Antioch was bigger than that."],[662.54,"Oh yeah. Um Well I've heard I've heard estimates for Rome and Alexandria as high as a million, but most estimates are less than that."],[673.34,"Yeah. Uh Antioch is just behind those two."],[676.86,"Yeah. And those are full-time residents."],[681.5,"There were almost there were almost as many, and this is going to become important later in the book of Acts."],[688.9,"There were almost as many Jews living in Antioch as there were in Jerusalem."],[695.7,"At this time in history."],[711.22,"There was a district, the Kerateon, in Antioch, that was the Jewish district."],[716.66,"And that community was there for centuries."],[720.02,"I mean, into the fourth-fifth century it's there was a huge Jewish community there."],[727.38,"So yeah, the population was in flux a lot depending on the feast as you get an idea from that."],[728.26,"You know where you'd have just crammed, you know"],[737.02,"Pentecost there were probably maybe 350,000 people there."],[742.7,"So 3,000 is a big number but it's not as if it was like everyone there."],[749.82,"You know, it was less than one percent you know of the people."],[753.5,"It's a huge number of people but you know in terms of balance you know and we we aren't told we we've been saying, and and I should correct this, we've been saying there are 8,000 people."],[767.86,"We are told that all 8,000 of them stayed in Jerusalem."],[771.34,"That's true. Either."],[773.38,"We get these big numbers, but remember this transient population."],[777.3,"There are probably a lot of those people who went back to wherever they were from."],[782.5,"Because they were there for Pentecost."],[784.2,"And so, and we're gonna find again later on in the book of Acts when St."],[787.96,"Paul goes out, there are gonna be sort of people here and there who sort of are already Christians."],[795.72,"You know, he's gonna have people to stay with and stuff."],[798.52,"He's gonna have, you know, so uh St."],[801.4,"Barnabas, you know, is from Antioch."],[805.14,"But we don't read about him sort of converting or uh becoming part of the Christian community."],[813.86,"He's just sort of already is when they go to Antioch."],[816.74,"So a lot of these people sort of left the city."],[826.3,"So yeah, those are the people who aren't there."],[830.54,"Sort of the mainstream members of the community."],[833.82,"Word is spreading and Christianity is spreading beyond what we're actually reading about here."],[840.03,"Because of this dispersal."],[841.55,"We need to be slightly careful about that too, the way we think about it."],[845.39,"Uh-huh. Um, because like you just said, and I I've probably said it the same way, so I'm not criticizing."],[852.59,"We say Christianity is spreading."],[854.67,"We tend to look at it like Christianity is this new religion."],[857.83,"Uh-huh. Right now, and that these people are are Jewish people who are converting to Christianity."],[862.11,"And that there's not sort of separate religions right now"],[869.11,"Right now we're talking about at this point in Acts, we're talking about everybody's Jewish who we're talking about."],[875.35,"Both the believers and the non-believers are all Jewish."],[878.95,"So we've got one group that has accepted that Jesus is the Messiah."],[884.31,"And we've got another group that doesn't accept."],[887.11,"We've got two groups of Jews."],[889.19,"A group of Jews who believe in Jesus as the Messiah and a group of Jews who do not, at this point."],[895.83,"And those two groups are going to become Christianity and what we call Judaism."],[904.39,"But that's later."],[906.07,"That's not in. 33 AD"],[914.27,"So, but that, and that is, as we saw from St."],[917.23,"Peter's sermon, that's the message they're preaching, is that Jesus, who was just crucified, rose from the dead, and is the Messiah."],[931.91,"Okay. So the idea is these other these other uh believers are sort of scared to join the apostles, so that's why there's a but there."],[944.87,"Uh-huh. But the actuality was that because of what was happening with the apostles, with their preaching and these miracles and these things that they were doing in public, the average people in Jerusalem, even the ones who weren't ready to sign on with the idea that Jesus was the Messiah, had respect."],[961.26,"Yeah, they're in practice."],[963.15,"And uh that they don't think, oh, who are these new heretics?"],[967.63,"You know, coming here with some weird religion or anything."],[971.47,"They they're people who are held in high esteem just by the general broad Jerusalem community."],[980.83,"Now believers were increasingly added to the Lord, multitudes of both men and women."],[987.67,"It's interesting to note that he mentions both men and women."],[992.67,"We talked a little bit last time when we talked about Ananias and Sapphira about the fact that and how significant it is that Sapphira didn't just drop dead when Ananias did."],[1005.85,"Which might have been what you would have expected at this point in history."],[1011.77,"Why? It was in particular."],[1012.89,"Women in general and wives in particular were not considered sort of a separate, separate from their husbands."],[1018.15,"So and and we know she was in on it with them."],[1020.87,"We were told she was in on it with them."],[1022.79,"So when he lied, they didn't both drop dead."],[1025.99,"But she came and St."],[1027.27,"Peter asked her directly."],[1029.65,"Did you add whether she also lied, then she so uh back in the Gospels, for example, we talk about the feeding of the 5,000, and if you actually read the text, it says there were 5,000, about 5,000 men, plus women and children."],[1046.81,"Uh-huh. Sort of, we just count the men, we don't know how many women and children are there."],[1052.33,"But notice here that St."],[1053.85,"Luke indicates both men and women, indicating them separately."],[1060.47,"That they're both their own accord."],[1062.32,"They're both coming and believing."],[1064.64,"And we're gonna see as we go through the book of Acts and in St."],[1067.28,"Paul's epistles, we're gonna see an inordinate number of women's names."],[1072.32,"Especially for something from the ancient world, uh-huh."],[1075.6,"Where they did they didn't talk about women a lot."],[1078.8,"And part of the reason for that, and this is important because it runs counter to the way people talk about Christianity today in our culture, is that a vast number of the early converts to Christianity."],[1092.28,"When I say converts here, I'm not primarily talking about Jews, I'm talking about Gentiles who convert to Christianity, were women and slaves."],[1106.44,"When I say world, I don't just mean the Roman world."],[1108.6,"I mean the world."],[1109.24,"You can go to China, you can go to India, you're not gonna find anything different."],[1113.56,"Considered slaves and women to be equally human as individuals to men, to free men."],[1121.96,"You mean they they didn't think of them as equally, no one else did."],[1125.64,"Yeah, Christianity did."],[1126.68,"Christianity taught that they were all equal in the sight of God, in terms of their salvation"],[1134.14,"And so that was immensely we use the language now of empowerment."],[1139.26,"That was immensely empowering at the time."],[1142.68,"To to the women, to slaves, to the poor, to, because uh again, they're being treated as full human beings with their own minds, were able to decide for themselves, were able to become disciples of Christ themselves, you know, and hear and understand these things."],[1161.14,"Um, a lot of, and we'll get to this when we get into St."],[1164.18,"Paul's epistles. There are a number of passages that have been kind of misinterpreted."],[1169.94,"Uh, one of the most famous ones is when St."],[1170.98,"Paul says that women should stay silent in church"],[1174.94,"If they have questions, they should ask their they should ask their husband."],[1179.26,"It's sort of misinterpreted as if uh St."],[1181.74,"Paul is saying that that uh women don't know enough to speak."],[1186.86,"That's not what he's saying at all."],[1189.18,"In the synagogues at this time, they were segregated by gender."],[1192.54,"And since they didn't think women could understand anything, it was complicated."],[1198.12,"They didn't expect them to listen or pay attention."],[1202.12,"So the men would go and hear the sermon and hear the scripture and do all the things, and the women would sort of hang out and talk in the back and visit, and you know that's and that was it."],[1212.92,"And St. Paul is saying, no."],[1215.24,"They need to hear what's being said too"],[1217.2,"No, they need to be here, they need to listen too."],[1220.4,"Uh huh. And if they have questions, they should ask their husband, and their husband should help them understand."],[1229.44,"Because it's important that the wife also understands these things."],[1234.05,"The way they would have looked at it is well, if the husband understands it, he gets it."],[1239.19,"He's the head of the family."],[1241.03,"So if he becomes a Christian, the whole family's Christian just automatically."],[1244.87,"No. That's how they would have viewed it in their head."],[1247.47,"Say Paul is saying that's not how it works."],[1251.07,"We do read of people being baptized and their whole household with them."],[1255.49,"Yeah. But well, we'll talk when we start getting to those baptisms."],[1257.89,"Yes, okay But but uh see, we we have this idea that that the the these people didn't go through a lengthy period of catechesis before they were baptized."],[1272.25,"It wasn't like, okay, once you've learned and understand all these things, then we'll baptize you."],[1278.25,"Bring you into the church."],[1279.45,"It was they baptized you and brought you into the church, and then you started learning these things."],[1286.65,"Okay. And so St."],[1288.33,"Paul is saying, no, the women need to learn, and and and the husband and the wife need to teach the children these things."],[1295.19,"The children need to learn these things."],[1297.51,"Everyone needs to learn and come to understand these things, not just the men who are head of. a household"],[1303.63,"If you were to watch many of these the liturgies of many ultra-orthodox um synagogue liturgies, it is like that."],[1313.15,"There is a curtain that separates the women from the men."],[1316.73,"And uh it's still a tradition still held to this day."],[1319.45,"Yeah. And I was dumbfounded."],[1321.93,"I went into the cathedral in Athens, which isn't very big."],[1325.53,"Yeah. Uh uh with a bunch of students, and we we we all sat down."],[1331.05,"And after a while we began to realize that the men were on one side of the aisle on the other side of the aisle."],[1339.29,"Yeah. That came from a different place."],[1342.07,"And it isn't because the women aren't supposed to listened, it's because both are supposed to listen and not be. looking at and involved with each other during the service so that everybody can focus"],[1354.03,"Um even in our church in Bethlehem, like men will sit down in the first rows and women to the back."],[1361.79,"And this this is not anything to do with the men's uh or women."],[1365.95,"It's just to separate them, as you said, it's just not to flutter with each other or it's just you pay attention to what you hear, and the majority will be women, more than to be honest."],[1377.15,"More scenes will be for women."],[1378.99,"Yeah, and that's what that's what you find in the ancient world that was peculiar to Christianity."],[1384.27,"Uh-huh. Because Christianity was the only religious view going that said that women should. should not just could, but you know, come and learn these and accept themselves"],[1398.23,"And so it's very significant that St."],[1399.91,"Luke says that."],[1401.91,"That these people were coming to believe, both men and women were coming to believe."],[1407.59,"You know, these people were coming to believe in Jesus."],[1409.91,"And remember, that's what it's about."],[1411.19,"It's about accepting Jesus as the Messiah, because everybody here is Jewish."],[1415.83,"That's what they're talking about, coming to believe."],[1424.23,"Okay. And multitudes of both men and women."],[1426.87,"So now we're gonna lose count."],[1429.55,"I just know it's a lot."],[1430.83,"We don't know exactly how many."],[1434.35,"So that they brought the sick out into the streets. and laid them on beds and couches that at least the shadow of Peter passing by might fall on some of them"],[1443.95,"So, you know, this has become so well known."],[1448.35,"So well known what the apostles are doing is so well known in the city."],[1452.05,"It doesn't say all these people were believers necessarily."],[1455.25,"But everybody was going and hey, I have a cousin who's sick over here."],[1458.61,"I'm going to bring him, you know, to see to see the apostles so that they could be healed."],[1464.45,"And even if, you know, he they don't have time to lay hands on everybody, they don't have time to do it."],[1469.73,"Well, maybe just as he walks by, you know, we'll just get him close, you know, and maybe uh maybe they'll be healed."],[1480.77,"Also, a multitude gathered from the surrounding cities to Jerusalem, bringing sick people and those who are tormented by unclean spirits, and they were all healed."],[1490.89,"Okay, so it gets around the city so much that even people from those villages, you know, Bethany and all these places around, start bringing their people into the city to see them."],[1499.93,"So so Peter's shadow works."],[1504.54,"Well, well, God is healing people."],[1509.34,"Yeah. Through St."],[1510.99,"Peter. But yeah, yeah."],[1513.31,"Well, well, no, but part of part of the significance of that is to indicate that it's not Peter."],[1518.27,"Uh-huh. Yeah. Because Peter's not even looking at this person."],[1522.16,"Yeah. Uh-huh. It's not that Peter has this. magical power to heal people"],[1526.64,"It's that God is bringing heal Christ in particular is continuing to heal people, which he did in the Gospel of Luke."],[1534.96,"He's continuing to heal people now through Peter and the other apostles."],[1538.8,"And that's the way how people believe."],[1540.72,"If somebody's healed, that will gather hundreds and thousands of people to believe."],[1545.92,"Yeah, well, because if if you know the you have someone who's been suffering, you know, their whole life with some illness or handicap, and you bring them to this person, and that and they're better, and then that person says, Well, let me tell you."],[1561.8,"The reason I was able to do this is because I'm a follower of Jesus who's the Messiah."],[1566.72,"You're probably gonna listen to what he has to say at that point, you know."],[1567.92,"And you will spread the world"],[1572.65,"And then you'll go telling your friends and your family, and then they'll say, Oh, well, you know, I have a cousin in this village who he has this problem, maybe, you know, and they'll bring them, and then you know, and so so not only not only is all this happening in the community is growing, but the Christian community is developing this reputation among the whole city and the whole people."],[1599.61,"Then the high priest rose up, and all those who are with him, which is the sect of the Sadducees, and they were filled with indignation."],[1608.09,"Okay, so the uh we talked last time a little bit about the high priest and the Sanhedrin, the Sadducees."],[1613.21,"and The Sadducees are the ones who had control of the temple the priesthood."],[1619.89,"Uh of course the high priest was uh one of them who had been elected."],[1624.13,"They were sort of collaborators with the Romans and were primarily concerned with sort of holding down their own power."],[1629.62,"And if this other community is sort of developing this sort of charismatic power, where people are going to see them and hear them preach."],[1641.61,"And we've heard they're already, though they're praying at the temple, they're also praying together."],[1646.49,"They're also living in common."],[1648.35,"So we're already presumably starting to get the Eucharist being celebrated."],[1653.4,"In addition to the synagogue and temple services."],[1656.53,"That's now, and people are bringing money."],[1659.81,"The Sadducees really like money."],[1662.93,"That's going away from the temple and over to this group."],[1669.65,"So this is why they're indignant."],[1672.77,"You say, well, why would they be upset?"],[1674.45,"People are getting healed."],[1675.49,"People are, you know, good good things are happening."],[1678.61,"Well, it's not good for them."],[1681.22,"Because money and power are moving away from them and over to these others."],[1688.42,"And they laid their hands on the apostles and put them in the common prison."],[1693.54,"Okay. Now the the common prison is referring to, remember, we talked about them locking up. Saints Peter and John"],[1701.5,"They don't have the authority to put them in actual prison."],[1705.76,"Roman prison. Because they're not that authority, but they can sort of govern their own affairs."],[1712.26,"And so this is sort of holding cells."],[1714.9,"This is their prison."],[1716.11,"Holding cells where guarded by the temple guard, where presumably they can have again some kind of trial or hearing with the apostles."],[1727.63,"But at night an angel of the Lord opened the prison doors and brought them out and said, Go stand in the temple and speak to the people all the words of this life."],[1738.87,"It's kind of a wonky translation of what the angel said."],[1743.13,"All the words of this life."],[1745.39,"They probably should have here in the Orthodox Study Bible capitalized life there."],[1754.51,"And even the this is kind of hazy."],[1759.23,"What it's talking about is it's talking about eternal life."],[1761.95,"It's talking about right, the the way of life of Christians."],[1771.47,"San Hendred says the temple guard, grabs them, throws them in these holy cells, angel comes, lets them out, and says, Go back out into the temple and start preaching again."],[1782.99,"Wow. And when they heard that, they entered the temple early in the morning and taught."],[1787.39,"the Okay, so apostles say."],[1792.95,"Alright, and they go and they start doing it."],[1796.55,"But the high priest and those with him came and called the council together with all the elders of the children of Israel and sent to the prison to have them brought."],[1809.59,"This is one place where a lot of modern translations want to be gender neutral."],[1816.87,"So they take where it says like sons of Israel and translate it as children of Israel."],[1822.23,"But you kind of miss the point here."],[1823.91,"This is the elders of the sons of Israel because Rebecca Israel was a person who had twelve sons."],[1829.85,"Who are the twelve tribes."],[1831.37,"So the idea is that this isn't now just the Sanhedrin in Jerusalem"],[1837.99,"This is uh we see the situation escalating."],[1841.59,"So they're hauling in elders from villages."],[1846.96,"Everybody. So that's why it says the whole council."],[1850.8,"The head people from the head men."],[1853.92,"Everybody who's nearby enough to uh get there in short order."],[1859.54,"So they're not just convening their own little group."],[1861.82,"The'yre bringing in everybody, all the rabbis, all the right teachers of the law."],[1868.18,"So on this point, they are bringing everybody before they know that the disciples are out of prison, or they think no, know they."],[1876.02,"No, the wait a minute"],[1876.06,"They've seen the disciples are now back out of prison and they're preaching again."],[1881.66,"Uh because it says they sent to the prison to have them brought."],[1885.18,"Oh no, you're right, you're right."],[1886.3,"Um so they don't know yet."],[1887.5,"Yeah. They they're bringing everybody in to have the trial that they were that they put them in prison because they were planning to have."],[1895.02,"Oh, okay, so that's what they did."],[1896.54,"They're getting everything, they're getting everybody."],[1899.34,"Uh-huh. Everybody. Because, when it was just St."],[1903.44,"Peter and St."],[1904.4,"John. Just the two of them."],[1906.63,"Their own little group just, you know, called it basically said stop it."],[1912.12,"And threatened them with a bunch of stuff, but they couldn't really do anything because they didn't have the authority to do anything beyond that."],[1918.76,"Now the situation is escalating."],[1919.0,"they And so bring in everybody."],[1919.08,"'re They like, this is a real problem that we need to deal with."],[1926.22,"And that's a lot."],[1927.02,"If we remember when they started building the temple and they started gathering the the different uh tribes from here and there, and they were giving us a count."],[1937.5,"Yeah. That was a huge number that we were talking about."],[1941.58,"The people who joined the Sanhedrin was 70 people."],[1946.14,"So this is that plus more."],[1949.82,"So this is this is a big group."],[1954.38,"Okay. And then they and then they sent to the prison to have them to have them brought in."],[1961.82,"But uh it's also significant, remember that in terms of the sons of Israel."],[1963.82,"the Israel has 12 sons, 12 tribes, there's also 12 apostles."],[1972.48,"Oh So we're seeing sort of a right because what's happened is remember what Jesus said to his disciples."],[1984.57,"When I come in my table, you'll sit on twelve thrones and judge the twelve tribes of Israel."],[1991.59,"So the apostles are now taking the place of the Sanhedrin, the elders, from the Old Testament."],[1999.12,"So St. Luke is trying to bring that out."],[2001.76,"That what they're trying to set up here is they're planning to judge the apostles."],[2006.3,"But in actuality, it's the apostles who now have the authority."],[2011.8,"And they're at least sort of recognizing that that's why they had them arrested."],[2016.36,"Because the apostles are sort of taking this authority away from them in the eyes of the people of Jerusalem."],[2025.24,"When the officers came and did not find them in the prison, they returned and reported saying, indeed, we found the prison shut securely and the guards standing outside before the doors."],[2034.84,"But when the op when we opened them, we found no one inside."],[2039.4,"So the guards are standing there, everybody, everything seems to be okay, but they go and they open the door and you and nothing."],[2046.2,"There's nobody in there."],[2047.08,"It must have been a little upsetting to report that."],[2049.72,"Yeah. Well, we'll see now when the high priest the captain of the temple and the chief priest heard these things they wondered what the outcome would be again that's an interesting translation they were sort of dumbfounded right they're like what is going on right that's they disappeared a little confused they said the angel opened the doors of the prison and let them out and let them out and here the doors are securely locked yeah so he closed it again after them."],[2083.72,"Oh, okay. It put everything back yeah to rights but yeah okay but wasn't there a gourd?"],[2092.52,"Yeah, there was plenty of guards as well."],[2094.52,"Yeah, so they must have been put to sleep or didn't see, or angels can do that kind of thing."],[2102.84,"This is a very neat angel who put everything back just to the other."],[2107.48,"I mean they got off a lot better than the guards at Jesus II."],[2111.0,"Yeah. Who fell down as if dead."],[2121.32,"So one came and told them saying, look, the men whom you put in prison are standing in the temple and teaching the people."],[2127.32,"So while they're trying to figure out what's going on, somebody comes running in and says, Hey, remember those guys you arrested last night?"],[2133.88,"They're out there teaching in the temple again."],[2138.36,"Then the captain went with the officers and brought them without violence, for they feared the people lest they should be stoned."],[2144.82,"So the guards, they send the guards, they tell the captain, you go and you arrest them again."],[2149.96,"And the guard captain's like, okay, guys, we need to do this quietly and peacefully because they had such a good reputation."],[2159.89,"They worried if they came in and, you know, started knocking heads and grabbing people around that the people would turn on them."],[2165.81,"You know, why are you, you know."],[2167.25,"It also shows that the apostles are not resisting violently."],[2172.21,"They're going with them without any problem."],[2176.07,"But that shows you just how much the public opinion had shifted."],[2180.95,"Yeah. In terms of how the people of Jerusalem view the apostles and how they view the temple guards and the Sanhedrin, who those guards represent."],[2189.33,"That if it came down to a conflict, the people would all take the apostles' side."],[2193.17,"And the situation was becoming was escalating again."],[2198.4,"And take the apostles' side to the point that the guards were scared they'd be killed."],[2202.24,"Uh-huh. If they the people would kill them."],[2206.26,"Not just the people would go and pick it."],[2208.5,"Uh-huh. But the people might kill them if they were seen to oppose the apostles."],[2216.34,"When they had brought them, they sent them before the council, and the high priest asked them, saying, Did we not strictly command you not to teach in this name?"],[2224.02,"And look, you have filled Jerusalem with your doctrine and intend to bring this man's blood on us."],[2227.94,"So what's interesting is we don't sort of get to their real issue until the end"],[2236.14,"They say, First, we told you not to do this, didn't we?"],[2239.58,"Which, of course, we know is true."],[2241.02,"They did, in fact, tell them not to do this."],[2244.38,"And you remember what the answer was at the time."],[2246.3,"St. Peter and St."],[2247.26,"John said, Well, should we obey men or should we obey God?"],[2251.58,"Uh huh. Kind of not a way around that one."],[2258.62,"They said, Now look, you know, you've preached this all over Jerusalem."],[2261.58,"All these people are following your thing."],[2263.34,"And then we get to the end, we get to the real crux."],[2265.5,"You're trying to bring this man's blood on us."],[2267.92,"Well, didn't you?"],[2269.46,"Yes. Two weeks ago, they're not going to be able to do that."],[2272.74,"Well, the the right, but the the the idea is that they're saying that Jesus was the Messiah, that Jesus was innocent."],[2282.74,"And that they murdered him."],[2285.15,"From their perspective, they weren't murderers."],[2287.85,"They still don't think Jesus is the Messiah."],[2289.93,"They think he was a false prophet."],[2292.33,"And so they were right to kill him."],[2294.51,"It's not that they're saying we had nothing to do with killing him."],[2298.97,"They're not saying, oh, that was the Romans."],[2300.65,"We don't know what you're talking about."],[2301.77,"We had nothing to do with that."],[2303.19,"The idea of their blood being on that that they're guilty somehow of shedding an innocent person's blood."],[2309.51,"Okay. Which is a major thing, of course, in the in the Torah."],[2316.03,"Starting right after the flood."],[2318.28,"God says, He who spill spills man's blood, social blood be spilled by men."],[2323.66,"And uh, even earlier than that, after Cain killed Abel, when God comes to Cain, he says, Your your brother's blood cries out to me from the ground, you know, for vengeance for what you did."],[2336.8,"And so uh the problem is the high priest and the said editor see it is you're accusing us of murder."],[2345.62,"When you go out and preach this, you're accusing us of being of murdering an innocent man."],[2352.5,"There's all these thousands of people who seem to be agreeing with you."],[2356.68,"' And so, you know, you can imagine wed like you to leave off calling us murderers."],[2366.88,"And this isn't, remember again, this isn't just an issue of, you know, uh now we get into these debates and discussions about anti-Semitism about whether the Jews killed Jesus."],[2377.2,"This isn't about just Jewish people."],[2379.2,"These are the actual people."],[2382.4,"This is the same high priest who Jesus stood in front of not that long ago."],[2386.53,"So these are the actual individuals who were responsible for the death of Jesus."],[2394.29,"But Peter and the other apostles answered and said, we ought to obey God rather than men."],[2399.89,"We're not going to ask as a question this time"],[2400.87,"Remember what we said last time?"],[2402.31,"Uh-huh. We're just going to tell you straight out, we're going to obey God and not you."],[2409.31,"If what God tells us to do and what you tell us to do conflict, we're going with God."],[2416.67,"The God of our fathers raised up Jesus whom you murdered by hanging on a tree."],[2422.19,"Just to put it bluntly."],[2423.55,"So once again, we're saying."],[2424.8,"So when he says that the God of our fathers raised up Jesus, he's saying Jesus is the Messiah."],[2429.44,"Jesus came from the God of Israel."],[2432.74,"Our people's God who we worshiped."],[2434.9,"He raised up Jesus as the Messiah."],[2437.3,"You guys, you people in this room, you murdered him."],[2441.75,"And the phrase, it doesn't just say you crucified him, you murdered him by hanging him on a tree, is going back again to the Torah."],[2441.85,"And you murdered him."],[2450.65,"Cursed is everything which hangs on a tree in Deuteronomy."],[2456.33,"Um that was a curse in the book of Joshua after after uh they take the city of Ai."],[2463.61,"The city of Ai had had uh opposed them and and rejected and sort of mocked Israel's God."],[2472.33,"And so when they take the city, they take the king and they kill him and they leave his body hanging on a tree is a curse."],[2479.53,"So they not only did you murder Jesus, who was the Messiah."],[2484.79,"But you cursed him."],[2485.43,"curs Youed him, you hated him."],[2485.91,"ed him. And you murder"],[2491.94,"So remember, this is the follow-up to we're going to obey God, not you."],[2496.74,"Why are we going to obey God, not you?"],[2498.58,"Well, because you're opposed to God."],[2500.98,"You took God's Messiah and you murdered him and you cursed him."],[2505.94,"So we're not really interested in what you have to say religiously anymore."],[2515.78,"Him, God has exalted to his right hand to be prince and savior, to give repentance to Israel and forgiveness of sins."],[2525.54,"So, this is what you did."],[2528.18,"God raised him as Messiah, you murdered himed. him and curs"],[2532.38,"God raised him up and now has enthroned him in his right hand."],[2540.62,"And because of him, repentance and forgiveness of sins has come to the people."],[2546.94,"And so that's how now St."],[2549.66,"Peter is characterizing what's happening with the people."],[2554.38,"Why is this important?"],[2555.9,"Because they're treating it as, oh, you're starting this movement."],[2560.16,"Your doctrine, your opinions that you're going and spreading around."],[2564.26,"Trying to build this following for yourselves."],[2566.82,"And St. Peter is saying that's not what's happening."],[2569.8,"What's happening is because of Jesus, repentance and forgiveness of sins is coming to these people."],[2574.36,"And believing in Jesus and following us"],[2574.96,"That's why they're all coming."],[2580.0,"Not because we're trying to put together a movement to get ourselves rich over against you guys who are here to get yourself rich."],[2590.16,"And we are his witnesses to these things, and so also is the Holy Spirit, whom God has given to those who obey him."],[2598.24,"Remember, in the Old Testament, to establish that something is true, you needed two witnesses."],[2607.44,"And the two witnesses had to say the same thing."],[2610.08,"So they're putting the apostles on trial."],[2612.08,"St. Peter says, This is what is true."],[2614.72,"I got two witnesses."],[2616.8,"Us. The apostles, who saw you killed Jesus, saw that he was the Messiah, saw you kill him, saw him rise again, saw him ascend into heaven to be seated at the right hand of God."],[2628.85,"We saw this, so we're witnesses and the Holy Spirit."],[2632.37,"What is now made of their witness of this remnant of the Holy Spirit."],[2641.47,"Well, in the Old Testament, we saw on the day of Pentecost when the Holy Spirit came, and St."],[2648.61,"Peter preached from uh chapter two of the book of Joel."],[2651.73,"Remember, talked about the Holy Spirit coming upon all flesh."],[2655.51,"And that was as opposed to in the Old Testament, where only certain individuals had the Holy Spirit."],[2662.15,"So Moses. had the Holy Spirit"],[2664.75,"And then there's that episode in Numbers where a portion of the spirit is put onto the 70 elders and they also prophesy."],[2673.79,"But that's just for a short time."],[2675.81,"And then Moses says, Would that everyone could."],[2678.61,"We read that reading before Pentecost on at Vespers in Numbers."],[2684.45,"And so we read, you know, Saul, when he's the king, the Holy Spirit comes upon him, and then at a certain point leaves."],[2691.57,"And then the Holy Spirit comes upon David, and you know, in Psalm 50, read in Matt's, he says, Take not your Holy Spirit from me, because after he sinned, after he murdered Uriah and married his wife, he realized, Yeah, I've sinned."],[2705.17,"God could now take the the spirit from me, God could now abend me way he abandoned Saul."],[2711.45,"So he's praying, don't do that."],[2713.13,"But what you see in all those examples is who is it who has the spirit?"],[2716.97,"It's these leaders."],[2718.94,"It's it's Moses."],[2721.36,"It's the other prophets, it's the king."],[2724.16,"Um, and so the the Holy Spirit is is the one who sort of gives that person authority and makes them the leader of the people."],[2734.54,"And so when St."],[2735.66,"Peter says that the Holy Spirit is the second witness, whom God has given to those who obey Him."],[2742.44,"He's saying anybody."],[2744.4,"We have the spirit, not you."],[2746.96,"Uh-huh. Which means who who are the real leaders? of God's people"],[2753.2,"Us, not you."],[2755.6,"And because you've been disobedient, about as disobedient as you get, uh-huh, by murdering the Messiah, and you know, that's about cursing him."],[2765.92,"That I mean, there's not much past that, that you could do in terms of disobedience to God."],[2770.58,"Uh, because you've been disobedient, you now no longer have that authority from God to speak on these matters."],[2781.78,"And so that's sort of a last little dig."],[2787.38,"The second witness is the Holy Spirit, which you wouldn't have access to."],[2793.07,"Who doesn't indwell you but has come and indwell.ed our community"],[2799.83,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God."],[2807.19,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecouncil at ancientfaith.com."],[2812.55,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.2,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: where we are in Acts","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at <b>Acts 5:12</b>; first Acts study posted online with his <b>intro to the whole book</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Still in the <b>very early chapters</b>; recently: <b>way of life of the early community</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Community in Jerusalem = <b>continuation of the life of Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Acts 1: previous book was all Jesus <b>\"began to do and teach\"</b> - apostles continue</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>miracles</b> like Jesus' miracles; <b>teaching in the temple</b> like Jesus</li><li class=\"d1\">also the <b>Jewish authorities</b> who killed Jesus now coming after apostles - hauled before <b>Sanhedrin</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Exactly what Jesus promised (John): <b>\"if the world hated me, it will hate you\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if they persecuted me, they'll persecute you; if they listened to me, they'll listen to you</li><li class=\"d0\">Still in <b>Jerusalem</b> - first stage of ascension mission plan</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Jerusalem → Judea → Samaria → ends of the earth</b></li></ul>"},{"t":160.52,"lv":3,"h":"Last time: Ananias and Sapphira","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Parallel to <b>Leviticus</b>: God's presence enters tabernacle → <b>Nadab and Abihu</b> take it lightly, struck dead</li><li class=\"d1\">shows community this is <b>serious</b>: God living in their midst</li><li class=\"d0\">Same here: Holy Spirit indwells community → <b>Ananias and Sapphira</b> lied</li><li class=\"d1\">Peter: lied not to men but to the <b>Holy Spirit</b> now indwelling the community</li><li class=\"d1\">dropped dead, carried out - \"happy note\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Community grown from <b>~120 → ~8,000</b>, but still all within Jerusalem</li></ul>"},{"t":265.16,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:12-13 - Signs and wonders in Solomon's porch","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Many signs and wonders</b> through apostles; <b>one accord in Solomon's porch</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not a one-off (Peter and John healing the <b>paralyzed man</b> at the temple gate)</li><li class=\"d1\">like Gospels: \"Jesus went and healed the sick and drove out demons\" - <b>regular thing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Word <b>sign</b> (John): not a neat thing to draw attention - <b>points to something</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Jesus' signs → he is <b>Messiah</b>, Messianic Age beginning</li><li class=\"d1\">same now: <b>kingdom of God</b> beginning to take shape here</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Solomon's porch</b> = part of the temple</li><li class=\"d1\">no longer <b>hiding in a room</b>; done <b>publicly, in full view</b></li><li class=\"d1\">makes sense if they're signs: people of Jerusalem meant to see and be drawn</li><li class=\"d1\">evidence for preaching: all the Messiah things are happening → <b>\"they must be telling the truth\"</b></li></ul>"},{"t":373.23,"lv":3,"h":"Q: who \"dared not join them\"?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: \"none of the rest dared join them\" yet \"believers increasingly added\" - who are the ones not daring?</li><li class=\"d0\">Apostles = the <b>leadership</b>, out there in force</li><li class=\"d0\">Other <b>Christians</b> hold back because of <b>resistance already happening</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not 8,000 in Solomon's porch</li><li class=\"d1\">telegraphs something coming soon in Jerusalem</li><li class=\"d0\">Meanwhile ordinary people - even those not signing on - hold apostles in <b>high esteem</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"who are these new heretics with a weird religion\"</li></ul>"},{"t":480.79,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: population of Jerusalem","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: how many people in Jerusalem then? 8,000 already big</li><li class=\"d0\">Varies by <b>time of year</b>; temple still standing</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Passover, Pentecost, Tabernacles</b>: Jews from all over the world</li><li class=\"d1\">estimates up to <b>a million</b> around the city at Passover - many camping, in villages like <b>Bethany</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Why everyone worried when Jesus came at Passover</li><li class=\"d1\">crowds → <b>riots</b> easy; \"kingdom of God is coming\" preacher might cause trouble with Rome</li><li class=\"d1\">why <b>Pilate</b> quickly executed Jesus though he found no guilt - feared a riot</li><li class=\"d0\">Normal resident population ~<b>150,000</b> incl. villages; <b>hub</b>, later squashed by the Romans</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Antioch</b> bigger than that?</li><li class=\"d1\">Rome, Alexandria estimates up to a million; <b>Antioch just behind</b></li><li class=\"d1\">almost as many Jews in Antioch as Jerusalem - important later in Acts; <b>Kerateon</b> = Jewish district, there into 4th-5th c.</li></ul>"},{"t":727.38,"lv":3,"h":"Pentecost numbers and the dispersal","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Pentecost maybe <b>350,000</b> there → 3,000 baptized = <b>under 1%</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Correction: we're <b>not told all 8,000 stayed</b> in Jerusalem</li><li class=\"d1\">transient crowd - many <b>went back home</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Later: Paul finds <b>Christians already</b> in cities, people to stay with</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Barnabas</b> from Antioch - no conversion story, already Christian</li><li class=\"d0\">Christianity spreading beyond what we read, because of this <b>dispersal</b></li></ul>"},{"t":840.03,"lv":3,"h":"Two groups of Jews, not two religions","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Careful: not \"new religion\" vs Jews converting</li><li class=\"d0\">At this point in Acts <b>everybody is Jewish</b>, believers and non-believers</li><li class=\"d1\">one group accepts <b>Jesus as Messiah</b>, one doesn't</li><li class=\"d1\">later become <b>Christianity and \"Judaism\"</b> - not in <b>33 AD</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Peter's message: <b>Jesus, just crucified, rose and is Messiah</b></li></ul>"},{"t":980.83,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:14 - Multitudes of men and women","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Believers increasingly added</b> to the Lord, <b>both men and women</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Ties to Sapphira: she did <b>not drop dead</b> when Ananias did</li><li class=\"d1\">wives not seen as <b>separate</b> from husbands; Peter asked her directly</li><li class=\"d0\">Feeding of the 5,000: <b>\"5,000 men, plus women and children\"</b> - women uncounted</li><li class=\"d1\">Luke here names men and women <b>separately</b>, each coming and believing <b>of their own accord</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Acts and Paul's epistles: <b>inordinate number of women's names</b> for the ancient world</li></ul>"},{"t":1078.8,"lv":3,"h":"Women and slaves in the early Church","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Vast number of early <b>Gentile converts</b> were <b>women and slaves</b> - counter to how culture talks about Christianity</li><li class=\"d0\">No culture - <b>Rome, China, India</b> - saw slaves and women as <b>equally human</b> to free men</li><li class=\"d1\">Christianity: <b>equal in God's sight</b> in salvation</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>empowering</b>\" - full humans with own minds, able to be <b>disciples</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Only religious view saying women <b>should</b> come and learn and accept for themselves</li></ul>"},{"t":1164.18,"lv":3,"h":"Paul: \"women should stay silent in church\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Misread as women don't know enough to speak - <b>not</b> what he says</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Synagogues segregated by gender</b>; women not expected to listen</li><li class=\"d1\">men hear sermon and Scripture; women <b>talk and visit in the back</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul: <b>\"no\" - they need to hear too</b>; ask husbands, who should help them understand</li><li class=\"d1\">old view: husband understands → <b>whole family</b> Christian automatically; Paul: not how it works</li><li class=\"d0\">Households baptized - later; <b>baptized first, catechized after</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Husband and wife teach <b>children</b>; everyone learns, not just the head of household</li></ul>"},{"t":1303.63,"lv":3,"h":"Q: separate seating in church","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Ultra-orthodox synagogues: <b>curtain</b> separates women and men - still today</li><li class=\"d0\">Orthodox cathedral in Athens: men one side of aisle, women the other</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>not</b> because women aren't to listen - both listen, <b>not looking at each other</b>, to focus</li><li class=\"d0\">Church in Bethlehem: men in first rows, women at back - just to avoid <b>fluttering</b>; majority women anyway</li><li class=\"d0\">Luke's point: both men and women coming to <b>believe in Jesus as Messiah</b> - everybody here is Jewish</li></ul>"},{"t":1430.83,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:15-16 - Peter's shadow","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Sick brought into <b>streets on beds and couches</b> so <b>Peter's shadow</b> might fall on some</li><li class=\"d1\">apostles' work so <b>well known</b> - \"I have a cousin who's sick\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not necessarily all believers</li><li class=\"d1\">no time to lay hands on everyone</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Multitude from surrounding cities</b> - <b>sick and tormented by unclean spirits</b> - <b>all healed</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Peter isn't even looking at them → <b>not Peter's magic power</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Christ</b> continuing to heal, as in <b>Luke's Gospel</b>, through Peter and apostles</li><li class=\"d0\">Healing gathers people to believe</li><li class=\"d1\">healed person says \"I'm a follower of <b>Jesus the Messiah</b>\" → you listen, tell friends and family</li><li class=\"d1\">community grows; develops a <b>reputation across the city</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1599.61,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:17-18 - High priest's indignation","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>High priest and the Sadducees</b> filled with indignation</li><li class=\"d0\">Sadducees: <b>control of temple and priesthood</b>, high priest elected from them</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>collaborators with Romans</b>; concerned to hold their own power</li><li class=\"d0\">New community has <b>charismatic power</b>; people go to see and hear them preach</li><li class=\"d1\">also <b>praying together, living in common</b> → Eucharist presumably already celebrated, beside synagogue and temple services</li><li class=\"d1\">people bringing <b>money</b> - \"Sadducees really like money\" - going away from temple</li><li class=\"d0\">Why upset at healings? <b>Money and power moving away</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Laid hands on apostles, put them in the <b>common prison</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no authority for Roman prison; <b>holding cells</b> guarded by temple guard, for a trial or hearing</li></ul>"},{"t":1727.63,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:19-21 - The angel frees them","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Angel of the Lord</b> opens prison doors by night: \"Go stand in the temple and speak to the people <b>all the words of this life</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"wonky translation\"; Orthodox Study Bible should capitalize <b>Life</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>eternal life</b>, the way of life of Christians</li><li class=\"d0\">Guard throws them in, angel lets them out, \"go back and start preaching again\"</li><li class=\"d0\">They enter temple <b>early in the morning</b> and teach</li></ul>"},{"t":1796.55,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:21 - Council convened with all the elders","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">High priest calls <b>council with all the elders of the children of Israel</b>; sends to prison to bring them</li><li class=\"d1\">modern translations go gender-neutral; really <b>sons of Israel</b> - <b>Israel had twelve sons</b>, the twelve tribes</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Escalation</b>: not just Sanhedrin - elders from villages, \"the whole council,\" rabbis, teachers of the law</li><li class=\"d1\">Sanhedrin = <b>70</b>; this is that plus more - \"a big group\"</li><li class=\"d0\">They don't yet know the apostles are out - sent to prison to fetch them</li><li class=\"d0\">Earlier just Peter and John: little group said stop it, threatened, couldn't do more</li><li class=\"d1\">now a <b>real problem</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1961.82,"lv":3,"h":"Twelve sons, twelve apostles, twelve thrones","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>12 tribes</b>, also <b>12 apostles</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Jesus: <b>\"you will sit on twelve thrones, judging the twelve tribes of Israel\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">apostles taking the place of the <b>elders/Sanhedrin</b> - Luke brings this out</li><li class=\"d0\">They plan to judge the apostles; <b>in actuality apostles have the authority</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why arrested them: apostles taking authority <b>in the eyes of the people</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2025.24,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:22-24 - The empty prison","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Officers report: prison <b>shut securely</b>, <b>guards standing outside</b> - opened it, <b>no one inside</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"must have been a little upsetting to report that\"</li><li class=\"d0\">High priest, captain of temple, chief priests <b>wondered what the outcome would be</b> - dumbfounded, \"what is going on\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Angel opened and <b>closed it again</b> - \"a very neat angel,\" put everything back</li><li class=\"d1\">guards put to sleep or didn't see - angels can do that</li><li class=\"d1\">got off better than guards at Jesus' tomb, who <b>fell as if dead</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2121.32,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:25-26 - Arrested again, without violence","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Someone runs in: <b>\"the men you put in prison are standing in the temple teaching\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Captain with officers</b> brings them <b>without violence</b> - feared the people would <b>stone</b> them</li><li class=\"d1\">do it \"quietly and peacefully\" - apostles' good reputation</li><li class=\"d0\">Apostles also <b>not resisting violently</b> - go along without problem</li><li class=\"d0\">Public opinion shifted: in a conflict <b>people take the apostles' side</b></li><li class=\"d1\">guards scared they'd be <b>killed</b> if seen to oppose the apostles</li><li class=\"d1\">situation escalating</li></ul>"},{"t":2216.34,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:27-28 - The charge: \"this man's blood on us\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">High priest: <b>\"Did we not strictly command you not to teach in this name?\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">true; remember Peter and John's answer: <b>obey men or obey God?</b> - \"no way around that one\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"You have filled Jerusalem with your doctrine\" - then the <b>real crux</b>: <b>\"bring this man's blood on us\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Their view: Jesus a <b>false prophet</b>, rightly killed</li><li class=\"d1\">not denying involvement (not \"oh, that was the Romans\")</li><li class=\"d1\">issue is being called guilty of shedding <b>innocent blood</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2309.51,"lv":3,"h":"Innocent blood in the Torah","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">After the flood: <b>\"whoever sheds man's blood, by man his blood shall be shed\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Cain and Abel</b>: \"your brother's blood cries out to me from the ground\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Apostles preaching = <b>accusing them of murder</b>; thousands agreeing</li><li class=\"d1\">they'd like it to stop</li><li class=\"d0\">Not about Jewish people in general or <b>anti-Semitism</b> debates - these are the <b>actual individuals</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same <b>high priest</b> Jesus stood in front of, responsible for his death</li></ul>"},{"t":2394.29,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:29-30 - \"We ought to obey God rather than men\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Not a question this time: <b>\"we ought to obey God rather than men\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">if God's word and yours conflict, <b>\"we're going with God\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"The God of our fathers raised up Jesus whom you murdered by hanging on a tree\"</b> - \"put bluntly\"</li><li class=\"d1\">= Jesus is <b>Messiah</b>, from the God of Israel they worship</li><li class=\"d1\">not just crucified: <b>\"hanging on a tree\"</b> → <b>Deuteronomy</b>: \"cursed is everything which hangs on a tree\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Joshua</b>: city of <b>Ai</b> mocked Israel's God; king killed, body hung on a tree as a <b>curse</b></li><li class=\"d0\">So: you murdered the Messiah <b>and cursed him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why obey God, not you: you're <b>opposed to God</b>; no interest in your religious say</li></ul>"},{"t":2515.78,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:31 - Prince and Savior","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"God has exalted to his right hand to be prince and savior, to give repentance to Israel and forgiveness of sins\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">You murdered him; <b>God raised him</b> as Messiah, <b>enthroned</b> at his right hand</li><li class=\"d0\">Because of him <b>repentance and forgiveness</b> come to the people</li><li class=\"d1\">answer to \"building a following for yourselves\"</li><li class=\"d1\">people come because of <b>Jesus</b>, not to get rich against you</li></ul>"},{"t":2590.16,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 5:32 - Two witnesses","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"We are his witnesses... and so also is the Holy Spirit, whom God has given to those who obey him\"</b></li><li class=\"d0\">OT: <b>two witnesses</b> must say the same thing; apostles on trial</li><li class=\"d1\">witness 1: <b>apostles</b> - saw the Messiah, saw you kill him, saw him <b>rise and ascend</b> to God's right hand</li><li class=\"d1\">witness 2: the <b>Holy Spirit</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2641.47,"lv":3,"h":"The Holy Spirit and God's leaders","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Pentecost: Peter preached <b>Joel 2</b> - Spirit on <b>all flesh</b>, vs OT where only certain individuals</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Moses</b>; <b>Numbers</b>: Spirit on the <b>70 elders</b>, they prophesy briefly; Moses: <b>\"would that everyone could\"</b> - read at Vespers before Pentecost</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Saul</b> had the Spirit, then it left; <b>David</b>, Psalm 50: <b>\"take not your Holy Spirit from me\"</b> after Uriah</li><li class=\"d0\">Pattern: the Spirit rests on the <b>leaders</b> - gives authority</li></ul>"},{"t":2734.54,"lv":3,"h":"\"We have the Spirit, not you\"","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Peter: Spirit given to those who <b>obey</b> - <b>we</b> have it, not you</li><li class=\"d1\">→ who are the <b>real leaders of God's people</b>? \"Us, not you\"</li><li class=\"d0\">You've been <b>as disobedient as you get</b> - murdered and cursed the Messiah</li><li class=\"d1\">→ no longer have <b>authority from God</b> to speak on these matters</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Last little dig\": second witness, the Spirit, you have no access to</li><li class=\"d1\">doesn't indwell you; <b>indwells our community</b></li></ul>"}]});
